{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race telemetry or integration feedback, so this is a baseline built from the contract. Five sensors are spread across the 25 mm tape: outer pairs at ±0.024 m and ±0.012 m, plus a centre sensor. With 12 mm footprints this gives overlap, so the tape is always seen by at least one sensor and the weighted signal changes smoothly as the line moves across the array. The sensors sit 0.05 m ahead of the axle, which gives the controller lead time on bends without putting them so far forward that they lose the line on tight turns. Wheel track 0.12 m and radius 0.03 m give a moderate yaw response and enough ground speed for the 1.5 m/s average needed to finish within 3 s. Body width 0.12 m keeps the off-track limit at its 0.06 m floor, which is the tight case, so the run ends quickly if the robot drifts. Mass 0.7 kg keeps inertia low for quick turn changes. Expected result: a first completion on the oval, with line-loss events low because the sensor overlap leaves no gap in the readings. Sensor weights are proposed as a symmetric pattern so the signal is antisymmetric about the centre line, which the Integrator can scale.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": 0.024, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.012, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.012, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.024, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.7
  },
  "intent": "Establish a symmetric five-sensor baseline with overlapping 12 mm footprints across the 25 mm tape and a sensor line 0.05 m ahead of the axle. The sensor set should give a signal that tracks line offset smoothly, and the moderate track and low mass should allow a fast enough run to complete within 3 s. Next iteration, use the Integrator's feedback to decide whether to move the sensors forward, widen the array, or change the wheel track.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "control_effort", "noise_robustness"]
  },
  "learning": "Baseline only. Hypotheses to test: (1) overlapping 12 mm sensors reduce line-loss events compared with spaced sensors; (2) forward sensor placement (0.05 m) reduces rms_error on curves at the cost of some jitter; (3) a 0.12 m wheel track is enough for stable turning without slipping at speeds needed to finish in under 3 s."
,
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor geometry",
      "notes": "Symmetric five-sensor array at 0.05 m ahead of the axle, with 12 mm footprints overlapping across the 25 mm tape, on a 0.12 m track and 0.7 kg body. No race evidence exists yet, so this is a contract-based baseline with hypotheses about line-loss and curve error to test."
    }
  }
}
